    [
      "heading",
      2,
      "result-and-persistence",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Result and persistence"
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Write mode performs a raw image write: it copies the ISO layout to the whole target device. It does not create an ext4 partition in unused space, create a persistence session, or perform a MiniOS Installer deployment. The filesystem choices above apply to Drive Utility operations that format a filesystem, not to the partition layout copied by an ISO write."
        ]
      ]
    ],
    [
      "block",
      "paragraph",
      [
        [
          "text",
          "Persistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Boot-Modes.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Boot modes"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " and "
        ],
        [
          "link",
          "/configuration/Initrd-Persistence.md",
          null,
          [
            [
              "text",
              "Initrd persistence"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "text",
          " before relying on saved changes."
        ]
      ]
    ]
  ],
  "plain_text": "Using Drive Utility\nDrive Utility is a graphical tool for writing MiniOS ISO images to USB drives.\nInstallation: Available in MiniOS by default, for other distributions see https://github.com/minios-linux/driveutility\nImportant\nWarning: Incorrect device selection will result in data loss! Always double-check the selected drive and backup important data.\nDrive Requirements\nDrive Size (for MiniOS writing)\nSee Hardware Compatibility Guide for detailed system requirements and drive sizes.\nSupported Filesystems\nFAT32: maximum compatibility\nNTFS: Windows compatibility\nEXT4: recommended for Linux\nLaunching Drive Utility\nThrough applications menu:\nOpen menu → System → \"Drive Utility\"\nThrough terminal:\ndriveutility\nCreating Bootable USB Drive\nSelect \"Write\" mode in the main program window\nSelect MiniOS ISO file:\nClick \"Browse\" button next to \"Source\" field\nFind and select the downloaded MiniOS.iso file\nSelect target drive:\nChoose your USB drive from the device list\nVerify selection by size and model\nStart writing:\nClick \"Write\" button\nConfirm operation - all data on the drive will be deleted\nWait for completion - process will take several minutes\nResult and persistence\nWrite mode performs a raw image write: it copies the ISO layout to the whole target device. It does not create an ext4 partition in unused space, create a persistence session, or perform a MiniOS Installer deployment. The filesystem choices above apply to Drive Utility operations that format a filesystem, not to the partition layout copied by an ISO write.\nPersistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See Boot modes and Initrd persistence before relying on saved changes.",
  "product_kind": "minios-markup-document",
  "schema_version": 1
}
